localtest: let OIDC_PLATFORM_URL carry a scheme. Upstream puts https:// in front of it in three places (the OIDC
plugin's and the token verifier's discovery, the /api/health check); the localtest stack serves Authentication over
plain http on local.altinn.cloud:8000. Without a scheme the value is used as upstream does, so production's
platform.<env>.altinn.cloud/authentication/api/v1/openid is unaffected.
Against Altinn/dialogporten-frontend bb74dff2c425f2aff48759ed9c6370e73436545d. Both Dockerfiles apply every patch in their source stage (git apply).

--- a/packages/bff/src/config.ts
+++ b/packages/bff/src/config.ts
@@ -66,6 +66,8 @@
   host: env.HOST,
   hostname: env.HOSTNAME,
   oidc_url: env.OIDC_PLATFORM_URL,
+  // localtest: a scheme in OIDC_PLATFORM_URL is kept (the localtest stack is plain http); upstream always prefixes https://
+  oidcDiscoveryUrl: `${/^https?:\/\//.test(env.OIDC_PLATFORM_URL) ? env.OIDC_PLATFORM_URL : `https://${env.OIDC_PLATFORM_URL}`}/.well-known/openid-configuration`,
   client_id: env.OIDC_CLIENT_ID,
   client_secret: env.OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET,
   platformBaseURL: env.PLATFORM_BASEURL,
